---
/**
 * Imprint (legal notice).
 *
 * Required for a site operated from Germany: Section 5 of the Digital Services
 * Act (DDG) and Section 18(1) of the Interstate Media Treaty (MStV). Written in
 * English because the whole site is; the statutes are cited by their German
 * names so a German reader can find them.
 *
 * The operator's details come from src/lib/legal.ts and nowhere else.
 */
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { OPERATOR, PRIVACY_HREF } from "@/lib/legal";
import { REPO } from "@/lib/install";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Imprint — Personal Jarvis"
  description="Legal notice for personaljarvis.ai: who runs this site and how to reach them."
  heading="Imprint"
>
  <p>
    Information pursuant to Section 5 of the German Digital Services Act
    (Digitale-Dienste-Gesetz, DDG) and Section 18(1) of the German Interstate
    Media Treaty (Medienstaatsvertrag, MStV).
  </p>

  <h2>Operator</h2>
  <address>
    {OPERATOR.name}<br />
    {OPERATOR.street}<br />
    {OPERATOR.city}<br />
    {OPERATOR.country}
  </address>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a></p>

  <h2>About this project</h2>
  <p>
    Personal Jarvis is a free, open-source project. Nothing is sold on this
    site: the software is published under the
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache License 2.0</a> and can be
    downloaded at no cost. This site has no editorial or journalistic content.
  </p>

  <h2>Consumer dispute resolution</h2>
  <p>
    We are neither obliged nor willing to take part in dispute resolution
    proceedings before a consumer arbitration board (Section 36 of the German
    Consumer Dispute Resolution Act, VSBG).
  </p>

  <h2>Liability for content</h2>
  <p>
    We write the content of these pages with care but cannot guarantee that it
    is complete, correct or current. As a service provider we are responsible
    for our own content under general law (Section 7(1) DDG). We are not
    obliged to monitor third-party information we transmit or store, or to
    investigate circumstances that point to unlawful activity (Sections 8 to 10
    DDG). Obligations to remove or block information under general law remain
    unaffected; liability of this kind begins only when we learn of a specific
    infringement, and we remove such content as soon as we do.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability for links</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to websites of third parties, such as GitHub, YouTube, X
    and Discord. We have no influence over their content, and their operators
    alone are responsible for it. We checked linked pages for obvious legal
    violations when we linked them. If we become aware of an infringement, we
    remove the link.
  </p>

  <h2>The software</h2>
  <p>
    Personal Jarvis is provided under the Apache License 2.0, which contains a
    disclaimer of warranty and a limitation of liability. Both apply to the
    extent permitted by applicable law; liability that cannot be excluded by
    law — for example for intent, or for injury to life, body or health —
    remains unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>Trademarks and copyright</h2>
  <p>
    Third-party names and logos shown on this site belong to their owners. They
    identify the services the software can connect to and do not imply any
    endorsement or affiliation. See the project's
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/TRADEMARK.md`}>trademark notice</a>.
    Content on this site that belongs to the project is published under the
    same licence as the software unless stated otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    How this site handles personal data is described in the
    <a href={PRIVACY_HREF}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
